Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 18:05:16 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Meridian: SessionTab/SessionWindow constructors no longer
 mint ids
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The constructors called SessionID::NewUnique, which writes a pref to local
state through PrefService and starts the ImportantFileWriter commit timer.
When the session commands are replayed off the main thread — which Meridian
does to read a Chrome profile for import — the timer started on a ThreadPool
worker with no sequence context and CHECKed (SIGABRT a minute into an
import-start launch, once the 10 s local-state commit timer had gone quiet).

The ids are data, not identity: the command replay (GetWindow/GetTab in
session_service_commands.cc) overwrites them right after construction, so
they now start at InvalidValue. Regression-tested by
chromium/tests/chrome_session_thread.test.mjs.
---
 components/sessions/core/session_types.cc | 10 +++++++---
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/components/sessions/core/session_types.cc b/components/sessions/core/session_types.cc
index 5e0a71f82b..452c899a0f 100644
--- a/components/sessions/core/session_types.cc
+++ b/components/sessions/core/session_types.cc
@@ -15,9 +15,13 @@ namespace sessions {
 
 // SessionTab -----------------------------------------------------------------
 
+// The ids are data, not minted here: the command replay (GetTab/GetWindow in
+// session_service_commands.cc) sets them right after construction, and minting
+// one would write a pref to local state — illegal off the main thread, where
+// the commands are replayed when Meridian reads a Chrome profile to import.
 SessionTab::SessionTab()
-    : window_id(SessionID::NewUnique()),
-      tab_id(SessionID::NewUnique()),
+    : window_id(SessionID::InvalidValue()),
+      tab_id(SessionID::InvalidValue()),
       tab_visual_index(-1),
       current_navigation_index(-1),
       pinned(false) {}
@@ -40,7 +44,7 @@ SessionSplitTab::~SessionSplitTab() = default;
 // SessionWindow ---------------------------------------------------------------
 
 SessionWindow::SessionWindow()
-    : window_id(SessionID::NewUnique()),
+    : window_id(SessionID::InvalidValue()),
       visible_on_all_workspaces(false),
       selected_tab_index(-1),
       type(TYPE_NORMAL),
